Z||000003||Formula88||04-30-2001||01:52 PM||||Could still be blowing a bit of oil if it is a BRAND new engine.  It takes a while for the engine to break in.  blowing oil isn't uncommon until the engine is fully broken in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||04-30-2001||01:59 PM||||I'm beginning to wonder if your choking the engine a bit to much. I remember to old rodchester quadrajunk carbs with bigger than necessary metering rods would cause whisps of smoke when ya got on it hard. Check the tailpipe and see if its really sooty maybe give her a hard run and pull out a plug while hot and see what color it is.. Just some ideas I came up with, this has to be the 5th post I have seen on this issue and this is the only logical explaination I can think of..||||reg||3
